d, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=\\frac{6-y}{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043025/assets/487b57182e190cbacf3b1ad30f55d227b59fb470e8b5609ad72327d229e53e45.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319190 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319191 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319192 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319193 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319194 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1041 "selection" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319191 13194139534911 true] [17592186319189 1110 #uuid "4613300a-55d0-58ab-b75b-f61da265b6df" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319190 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534911 true] [17592186319190 1111 #uuid "275db7fe-b720-5cb2-a4d0-b4c72eabddb5" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319191 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534911 true] [17592186319191 1111 #uuid "1791a065-628c-554c-b863-cb95eb42aa60" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319192 1034 "I only" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319192 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534911 true] [17592186319192 1111 #uuid "49f0d6b0-f8dd-526b-b88a-8e8c7c1089e5" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319193 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534911 true] [17592186319193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534911 true] [175